component ResourceManagement {
    goal {
        Manage rooms, room metadata, and base availability so room owners can
        publish spaces and Booking can check whether a requested time range fits
        those availability rules.
    }

    interface {
        A *Room* has a room identifier, display name, location, capacity, and
        optional amenities.

        A room owner can create a Room, update its metadata, publish it for search,
        or archive it.

        A Room's *base availability rules* describe recurring open periods and
        date-specific closures.

        Given a Room and a requested time range, Resource Management
        answers whether the entire range is permitted by that Room's applicable
        base availability rules.

        Room search returns available Rooms matching a supplied location and
        minimum capacity.
    }

    state {
        Resource Management owns Room, room metadata, and base availability rules.

        A Room can be draft, available, unavailable, or archived.
    }

    logic {
        A room owner publishes a draft Room with base availability rules to make it
        available for search.

        An available Room appears in search only when it matches every supplied
        filter.

        Resource Management reports a requested time range as available only when
        the Room is available, the full range falls within open periods, and the
        range does not overlap an applicable date-specific closure.

        Resource Management reports the requested time range as unavailable when
        the Room is not available, any part falls outside an open period, or the
        range overlaps an applicable closure.
    }

    constraints {
        Identity and Access supplies current-user and permission checks;
        Resource Management does not own users, sessions, roles, or permission
        policy.

        Resource Management's availability answer covers base availability rules.
        Booking owns conflicts with existing bookings and uses this answer when
        deciding whether to confirm a booking.

        Scheduling and Recurrence owns recurring booking patterns, series, and
        exceptions; recurring open periods remain base availability rules owned by
        Resource Management.
    }

    cases {
        A room owner publishes a Room with open periods and a date-specific closure.

        Booking asks whether a requested range fits an available Room's base
        availability rules and receives an available or unavailable answer.
    }
}
